Q: How do I make a piece of code run ONLY in the editor? A: <p>If I undertsand correctly the question isn't about how to run code only in the editor</p>
<p>The main issue here is rather that <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/Input.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Input</code></a> is only usable for code in playmode. While you are only in the editor this won't do anything.</p>
<p>Here you would rather need to use e.g. <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Event-current.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Event.current</code></a> and  instead directly hook into the <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/SceneView-duringSceneGui.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>SceneView.beforeSceneGui</code></a> callback via an <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/InitializeOnLoadMethodAttribute.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>InitializeOnLoadMethod</code></a></p>
<pre><code>#if UNITY_EDITOR
[InitializeOnLoadMethod]
private static void Init()
{
    SceneView.duringSceneView += HandleInput;
}

private static void HandleInput(SceneView _)
{   
    // To only do the thing during edit mode and ignore during play mode
    if(EditorApplication.isPlayingOrWillChangePlaymode) return;

    var ev = Event.current;

    if(ev != null &amp;&amp; ev.type == EventType.KeyDown &amp;&amp; ev.keyCode == KeyCode.B)
    {
        Debug.Log(&quot;Hello&quot;);

        // if you don't want the event to be further processed you have to consume it
        ev.Use();
    }
}
#endif
</code></pre>
<p>or alternatively if you need this for a non-static component you could use <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/ExecuteInEditMode.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>[ExecuteInEditMode]</code></a> and then hook up in e.g. <code>Awake</code> instead.</p>
<p>Or if this is an Editor-wide thing you want you could also use a <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/MenuItem.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>[MenuItem]</code></a> which allows to directly bind it to a shortcut as well .. though just using the B key would be quite bad in that case ;)</p>
<p>Now this should trigger only when hitting B while the SceneView is focused.</p>
